    "title": "Al Horford reveals new jersey number with Warriors - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tommy Call III ,\n2 hours ago Apr 29, 2025; Boston, Massachusetts, USA; Boston Celtics center Al Horford (42) warms up before game five of first round for the 2025 NBA Playoffs against the Orlando Magic at TD Garden. Mandatory Credit: David Butler II-Imagn Images By David Butler II, David Butler II-Imagn Images The Al Horford era in Golden State is officially underway. After an offseason filled with linked between the Warriors and the veteran center, Horford is slated to join Golden State after a four-year stint with the Boston Celtics.\nOn Wednesday, the Warriors officially introduced Horford as a member of the team. Along with answering questions from members of the media, Horford revealed his new Golden State jersey with a new number.\nAfter wearing No. 42 with the Celtics, Philadelphia 76ers and Oklahoma City Thunder, Horford picked No. 20 for his stint with the Warriors. Horford's previous number, No. 42, is retired with the Warriors in honor of Nate Thurmond. Horford also wore No. 42 in his college days with the Florida Gators. Horford also wore No. 15 early in his career with the Atlanta Hawks.\nVia @warriors on X:\nDario Saric was the last member of the Warriors to wear No. 20 in 2024. Other notable members of the Warriors to wear No. 20 include Jordan Bell, Kent Bazemore, James Michael-McAdoo, Larry Hughes, Terry Teagle and Phil Smith.\nOther new Warriors have also announced their jersey numbers. Seth Curry will wear No. 31 while De'Anthony Melton will wear No. 8 again. This post originally appeared on Warriors Wire ! Follow us on Facebook and Twitter !\nThis article originally appeared on Warriors Wire: Al Horford reveals new jersey number with Warriors",
